---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AISC Portfolio — Tryambak Kaushik" currentPath="/aisc/" description="Curated AISC portfolio work with reproducibility notes, exclusions, and project pages for recommender systems and reinforcement learning.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / AISC</p>
    <p class="eyebrow">AISC portfolio</p>
    <h1>Coursework and capstones, rebuilt as a <em>truthful public portfolio.</em></h1>
    <p>The original third-party publication pages are no longer available. This section restores the important work under my own domain and pairs it with the curated source repository, explicit exclusions, and reproducibility notes.</p>
    <div class="action-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/AISC" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open curated repository ↗</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/AISC/blob/main/PORTFOLIO_DATA_PROVENANCE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read provenance notes ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">Why this exists</p>
      <h2>Evidence, not performance.</h2>
      <p>The goal is not to make coursework look larger than it was. The goal is to present real work professionally: what was kept, what was excluded, how a reviewer can validate it, and where the limitations are.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <div class="detail-card"><strong>Kept</strong><span>Core notebooks, reports, and supporting artifacts that still help a reviewer understand the technical work.</span></div>
      <div class="detail-card"><strong>Excluded</strong><span>Large generated outputs, private credentials, trained weights, and third-party data copies that do not belong in a public repo.</span></div>
      <div class="detail-card"><strong>Documented</strong><span>Each exclusion is described so the repo does not imply completeness where it cannot honestly provide it.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">Featured case studies</p>
      <h2>Two rebuilt project pages are live now.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="project-grid">
      <article class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Recommender systems</span>
        <h3>BERT4Rec capstone</h3>
        <p>A sequential recommendation project using transformer-based modeling, paired with both the supporting report and the curated notebook set.</p>
        <div class="link-list">
          <a href="/aisc/recsys/">Read case study ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/AISC/tree/main/RecSys" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open repo folder ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Reinforcement learning</span>
        <h3>Financial forecasting notebook + paper</h3>
        <p>A stock-prediction project where the notebook contains the executable path and the report gives the narrative, framing, and results discussion.</p>
        <div class="link-list">
          <a href="/aisc/rl/">Read case study ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/tryambak2019/AISC/tree/main/RL" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open repo folder ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="note-card">
      <strong>What comes next</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>Additional AISC sections can be added for GANs, semi-supervised learning, MLOps, anomaly detection, and NLP.</li>
        <li>The repo remains the evidence layer; this site is the presentation layer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
